# WHAT `railway up` MUST NOT SHIP.
#
# The demo service builds from the monorepo root (its Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, then `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, then `turbo run build
# --filter=<app>`), so the upload is the whole tree. Untrimmed that is ~50MB of
# documentation, evidence media and eval corpora the build never reads — and a
# payload that size is what trips Railway's BadRecordMac upload failure.
#
# Only NON-package content is listed. Every workspace package's manifest has to
# survive this file or `--frozen-lockfile` fails on a missing workspace member,
# so heavy directories INSIDE a package (its docs/) are dropped rather than the
# package itself. `public/` is never touched: those files are served.
docs/
docs-site/
assets/
examples/*/docs/
packages/*/docs/
corpus/harness/src/knowledge-eval/fixtures/
